    j = j + "    \"L5: front radius is the ring-distance of the FARTHEST active cell from the seed centre; it measures the OUTER envelope of propagation, not a filled-front guarantee (interior cells may lag). C2 finite-speed is an envelope-speed claim. A filled-front (every interior cell active behind the front) claim would need a per-cell ignition-time map.\",\n"
